  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Outcomes, Results and Changes Evaluat</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The evaluation intends to generate learnings across the three (3) projects; The Power of Voices &#x2013; Fair for All Project (PvP - F4A),The DANIDA SP II project and the ICSP RISE-K project pioneering the nexus/OPA approach across the 4 themes of HumanitarianPreparedness &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Response, Resilient Livelihoods, Governance &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Accountability and Gender Justice &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Women&apos;s Rights programs.

Power of Voices Strategic Partnership Program FAIR for ALL In the FAIR for ALL Programme is one of the three projects embracing the nexus programming approach in OiU working towards achieving economic transformation that ensures that empowered smallholder coffee and horticulture farmers gain improved livelihood through inclusive and sustainable businesses.  We are also working towards adoptionof fair and equitable tax and public spending policies which not only spur the growth of agribusiness investments in Uganda, but also contribute to improving the livelihoods of the people especially the marginalized including women, youth, PWDs and further contribute to reducing inequality in Uganda.

The DANIDA SP II project similarly has a strong emphasis on nexus/OPA with support from DANIDA through Oxfam Denmark for contextualized Strategic Partners on Economic Justice and Inclusive democracies, Education for active citizenship, Inclusive peace building, Humanitarian Action &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Resilience to achieve a peaceful, gender and climate just society which upholds all human rights.

The ICSP-RISE-K (Irish Aid Civil Society Programme, Resilience, Inclusiveness, Stability and Empowerment of communities in Karamoja sub-region 2023-2027) is geared towards an empowered, inclusive, just, and resilient community in Karamoja sub region specifically geared towards improving governance and accountabilityfor effective service delivery in Karamoja subregion, improving gender relations and respect for the rights of women and other marginalized groups, enhancing local capacity for effective people-centered, climate and conflict-sensitive, gender-responsiveand inclusive disaster preparedness and response and enhancing adaptive capacity of women and youth to shocks and stresses for improved income, food, and nutrition security.</narrative>
  </description>
